cases.prompt:
Review three routes on ntdst-core 5.x:
  ntdst_rest('cache/v1')->post('/purge', $h);
  ntdst_rest('cache/v1')->post('/flush', $h)->public();
  ntdst_rest('shop/v1')->post('/orders', $h, ['permission' => 'edit_shop_orders']);
Which of these register, which do not, and what does a caller see on the wire for each? How is that third permission value actually evaluated?
